---
import type { Replay } from '../../scripts/backtest/replay';
import { pct } from '../../scripts/backtest/view';

interface Props {
  horizons: Replay['horizons'];
  decision: Replay['decision'];
  protocol: Replay['meta']['protocol'];
  headlineH: number;
}
const { horizons, decision, protocol, headlineH } = Astro.props;

const signed = (n: number, digits = 3) => (n > 0 ? `+${n.toFixed(digits)}` : n < 0 ? `−${Math.abs(n).toFixed(digits)}` : '0');
const hLabel = (h: number) => (h % 24 === 0 && h >= 168 ? `${h / 24}d` : `${h}h`);
const formulas = horizons[0]?.formulas.map((f) => ({ id: f.id, name: f.name })) ?? [];
const cell = (h: Replay['horizons'][number], id: string) => h.formulas.find((f) => f.id === id)!;
const head = horizons.find((h) => h.horizonH === headlineH)!;
const best = cell(head, decision.bestFormula);
const tone = (n: number) => (n > protocol.decisionMinSkill ? 'good' : n < 0 ? 'bad' : '');

const variantNote: Record<string, string> = {
  'no-buckets': 'Day-bucket floors dropped: the low end of the bid proxy',
  trusted: 'Only reads the live trusted-read rule keeps here (no bucket floors, no lower bounds)',
  'no-settle': 'Markets read until they close instead of stopping at the launch',
  uncensored: `Test ends ${protocol.admitDays} days before the pull, so no late rungs are missing`,
};
const primary = best.skill;
const variants = head.sensitivity.map((s) => ({ variant: s.variant, ...s.formulas[decision.bestFormula] }));
const bestVariant = Math.max(...variants.map((v) => v.skill));
const anySane = variants.some((v) => v.sane);
const noBuckets = variants.find((v) => v.variant === 'no-buckets');
/** The deciding formula and horizon lead, so they stay on screen when a phone scrolls the table. */
const scored = formulas
  .filter((f) => f.id !== 'base')
  .sort((a, b) => Number(b.id === decision.bestFormula) - Number(a.id === decision.bestFormula));
const columns = [...horizons].sort((a, b) => Number(b.horizonH === headlineH) - Number(a.horizonH === headlineH));
/** "(d) noisy-OR with unpriced rate u" → ["(d)", "noisy-OR with unpriced rate u"]. */
const nameParts = (name: string) => {
  const m = /^(\([a-z]\))\s*(.*)$/.exec(name);
  return m ? [m[1], m[2]] : ['', name];
};
const folds = decision.rollingSkill;
const foldVerdict = folds.every((s) => s > 0)
  ? 'every fold is above zero'
  : folds.every((s) => s <= 0)
    ? 'no fold is above zero'
    : 'the sign flips with the window, which is what a forecast with no stable edge looks like';
---
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Formula skill table">
  <table class="formulas">
    <caption class="sr-only">Out-of-sample Brier skill of each candidate formula against the fit-window base rate, with its 95% block-bootstrap interval and whether its reliability passed the sanity check, at each horizon.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Formula</th>
        {columns.map((h) => (
          <th scope="col" class={`num${h.horizonH === headlineH ? ' decide' : ''}`}>
            Next {hLabel(h.horizonH)}{h.horizonH === headlineH && ' · decides'}
            <span class="hsub">rate {pct(h.train.rate)} → {pct(h.test.rate)}</span>
          </th>
        ))}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {formulas.map((f) => (
        <tr class={f.id === decision.bestFormula ? 'best' : ''}>
          <th scope="row"><span class="fid">{nameParts(f.name)[0]}</span> <span class="fname">{nameParts(f.name)[1]}</span></th>
          {columns.map((h) => {
            const s = cell(h, f.id);
            return f.id === 'base' ? (
              <td class="num muted">0 <span class="ci">the reference</span></td>
            ) : (
              <td class={`num${h.horizonH === headlineH ? ' decide' : ''}`}>
                <span class={tone(s.skill)}>{signed(s.skill)}</span>
                <span class="ci">{signed(s.skillCi95[0], 2)} to {signed(s.skillCi95[1], 2)}</span>
                <span class={`flag${s.sanity.sane ? ' sane' : ''}`}>{s.sanity.sane ? 'sane' : 'fails sanity'}</span>
              </td>
            );
          })}
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="muted note">
  Skill is 1 − Brier ÷ Brier of (a), the fit window's base rate, on the held-out hours; above zero beats it. The small line is the 95% interval from a block bootstrap ({protocol.bootstrap.resamples.toLocaleString('en-US')} resamples of {protocol.bootstrap.blockH}-hour blocks). "Sane" means the mean forecast is within {protocol.sanity.maxMeanGap} of what happened and every bin with at least {protocol.sanity.minBinHours} hours is within {protocol.sanity.maxBinGap}. Rates are the share of hours with a frontier launch inside the horizon, fit window → held out.
</p>
<p class="rule">
  <span class="tiny glow-y">PRE-REGISTERED RULE</span>
  Ship a probability only if the best formula beats the base rate at {headlineH}h by more than {signed(protocol.decisionMinSkill, 2)} with sane reliability. The best was {best.name}: {signed(decision.skill)} (95% interval {signed(decision.skillCi95[0])} to {signed(decision.skillCi95[1])}), and its worst bin was off by {decision.worstBinGap.toFixed(2)}. <strong>Verdict: {decision.recommendation === 'lead-score' ? 'keep the hand-weighted lead score; the probability is context only' : 'ship the probability'}.</strong>
</p>

<h3 class="tiny sub" id="rolling">Rolling origin at {headlineH}h: fit on everything before each origin, test to the next</h3>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Rolling origin table">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Test window</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Launches</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Rate</th>
        {scored.map((f) => <th scope="col" class={`num${f.id === decision.bestFormula ? ' decide' : ''}`}>{f.name.slice(0, 3)}</th>)}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {head.rolling.map((r) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{r.origin.slice(5, 10)} → {r.testTo.slice(5, 10)}</th>
          <td class="num">{r.testEvents}</td>
          <td class="num">{pct(r.testRate)}</td>
          {scored.map((f) => <td class={`num ${tone(r.skill[f.id])}${f.id === decision.bestFormula ? ' decide' : ''}`}>{signed(r.skill[f.id])}</td>)}
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="muted note">
  {best.name.slice(0, 3)} scored {folds.map((s) => signed(s)).join(', ')} across the {folds.length} folds: {foldVerdict}.
</p>

<h3 class="tiny sub">Sensitivity at {headlineH}h (checked after the fact; none fed the verdict)</h3>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Sensitivity table">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Variant</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">{best.name.slice(0, 3)} skill</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">95% interval</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Sanity</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {head.sensitivity.map((s) => {
        const d = s.formulas[decision.bestFormula];
        return (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{s.variant}<span class="fname">{variantNote[s.variant] ?? ''}</span></th>
            <td class={`num ${tone(d.skill)}`}>{signed(d.skill)}</td>
            <td class="num">{signed(d.skillCi95[0], 2)} to {signed(d.skillCi95[1], 2)}</td>
            <td class="num">{d.sane ? 'sane' : 'fails'}</td>
          </tr>
        );
      })}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="muted note">
  The best variant reaches {signed(bestVariant)} against the primary read's {signed(primary)}, and {anySane ? 'some pass' : 'none passes'} the sanity check.{noBuckets && ` Dropping day-bucket prices alone moves it by ${signed(noBuckets.skill - primary, 2)}: they stand in for bids, and with no historical bid or ask the history can't say which read is right.`}
</p>
<style>
  .formulas th[scope='col'] { vertical-align: bottom; }
  .hsub { display: block; margin-top: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-xs); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; color: var(--muted); }
  th.decide, td.decide { background: rgba(255, 226, 28, 0.05); }
  tr.best th[scope='row'] { color: #fff; }
  .fname { display: block; font-size: var(--fs-xs); color: var(--muted); max-width: 34ch; }
  tr.best .fname { color: var(--text); }
  .ci, .flag { display: block; font-size: var(--fs-xs); color: var(--muted); }
  .flag.sane { color: var(--green); }
  .good { color: var(--green); }
  .bad { color: var(--red); }
  .note { margin-top: 8px; font-size: var(--fs-xs); max-width: 95ch; }
  .rule { margin-top: 14px; padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 226, 28, 0.45); max-width: 95ch; }
  .rule .tiny { display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .rule strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 400; }
  h3.sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 22px 0 8px; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
